                            <comment id="12893406" author="tdunning" created="Wed, 28 Jul 2010 22:46:32 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Here is the patch.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I will commit by EOD if nobody brings up a furball.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="12893425" author="tdunning" created="Wed, 28 Jul 2010 23:29:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I found my own furball.  Corrected patch.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="12893442" author="tdunning" created="Thu, 29 Jul 2010 00:25:00 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Tweaked a clone into a like and broke vector math.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fixed now.  Also slightly fixed the perceptron training that didn&apos;t count iterations correctly.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="12893459" author="jake.mannix" created="Thu, 29 Jul 2010 00:59:11 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hey Ted,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  I haven&apos;t had a chance to look at this code, but is it&apos;s operating on the purely in-memory matrices, right?  Not on DistributedRowMatrix yet?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="12893492" author="tdunning" created="Thu, 29 Jul 2010 04:04:06 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Correct.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is supporting my efforts at on-line learning which is entirely in memory.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="12893494" author="tdunning" created="Thu, 29 Jul 2010 04:07:01 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Jake,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I should say that aggregateRows and aggregateColumns would probably be very easy to get working on the DRM.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
